WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:09.990 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  ever since the dawn of mankind we've  wondered what happens to us once we run  out of extra lives is it simply game  over or is there a bonus level or  spectator mode afterwards is there a  part of us that persists even in death  ghost stories have been around since  ancient times in some cases the stories  are meant to be comforting the idea that  our ancestors watch over us on the flip  side ghosts have become synonymous with  themes of horror an angry vengeful  spirit who can stalk and sometimes even  kill its victim if you're not careful  there's no shortage of ghost stories and  they exist in pretty much every culture  that has ever been whether it's folklore  songs books tv shows or movies ghosts  are here to stay and the same thing goes  for video games the zelda series is no  exception they've appeared as early as  the very first installment and have  continued to do so all the way up to its  most recent titles the idea of life  after death is quite prevalent in zelda  and similar to real life it ranges from  something positive like meeting the  apparition of a deceased ally who helps  you in some way to negative experiences  like evil spirits who serve as enemies  or obstacles the games make it clear  that the deceased can sometimes linger  in this world and one pass on to the  afterlife until they have achieved some  sort of goal find peace or are destroyed  indefinitely usually by force in some  cases it can even be that the dead are  unable to rest because of a curse  something that binds them to the world  of the living making them unable to move  on until said curse is lifted they come  in all shapes and sizes but the most  famous rendition of ghosts in the series  are of course their pose they are said  to be spirits of the dead that became  monsters because of an unresolved  attachment to the mortal world the most  common of which are the feelings of  regret rage and hatred it's hard to  pinpoint the exact rules surrounding  these spirits as they aren't universal  and can sometimes differ slightly  depending on the game they are featured  in for instance in a link to the past  and ocarina of time they can manifest at  any time even in broad daylight whereas  in the wind waker and twilight princess  they only appear at night or in dark  places the sun doesn't reach like caves  and dungeons the wind waker especially  explains that pose hates sunlight  because it makes them vulnerable to  physical attacks their abilities also  differ slightly from game to game in  ocarina of time they can turn invisible  for small periods of time during which  attacking them is impossible in the wind  waker they can temporarily possess a  living host rendering them confused and  disoriented for a while and in twilight  princess they are invisible at all times  and can only be seen an attack by  wolfling when using his special senses  we've seen many different designs over  the course of the series from hooded  raves with glowing eyes mask hoodlums to  imp-like puppets wielding a scythe all  with their own looks personalities and  abilities but there's one thing these  menaces from the afterlife have in  common and that is that in a lot of  cases they are seen carrying a lantern  sometimes a torch there are exceptions  here and there but the lantern is  definitely a design choice that has been  carried over all across the series even  when the design of the creature itself  is vastly different it is also apparent  that the lantern or torch is an actual  physical object for instance in ocarina  of time when a po becomes invisible the  lantern is the only thing that remains  visible and upon defeating them the  lantern will fall to the ground and  shatter freeing the soul of the po which  can even be collected this process also  reveals the true form a spectral flame  burning in various colours most commonly  blue orange green and purple although  every game does its own thing and sets  different goals and limits when it comes  to the lore behind ghosts there's  definitely an overarching theme to be  found that being one of lanterns or  flames whenever ghosts or spirits are  involved but why is that is it just a  random design choice or is it based on  something like religion stories or  folklore as nintendo is often known to  do for instance the famous ghost hand  seen in skyward sword is derived from a  japanese ghost story a story about a  spirit named hanako who may reach up  from a toilet to snatch up an  unsuspecting victim well as you've  probably guessed yes the flames and  lantern are probably derived from real  life stories as well the most likely  candidate being an old legend which has  been passed down for many centuries  the willow the wisp or will in the wisp  is an atmospheric ghost phenomena first  documented in the english language by  william falk in 1563. starting with the  latin ignis fatus meaning foolish fire  the term has seen many different  translations meanings and  interpretations the stories involve  mysterious ghostly lights often  witnessed during night time by  travellers the most common description  is that of a pale blue flame moving or  dancing around in the distance they were  mostly seen in and around swamps and  marshes though some eyewitness reports  also include forests and even graveyards  although willow the wisp is the most  well-known version nowadays at least in  western culture similar stories have  existed all over the world each with  their own names meanings and stories  attached to it japan too has its own  share of similar stories like the onibi  hitodama and kitsune all of which  describe a similar phenomena of flames  balls of fire or mysterious lights  floating around at night because there's  so many similar legends and eyewitness  accounts of this phenomena from  different cultures naturally people had  different interpretations of what they  could be ranging from evil fairies to  witches elves and of course the souls of  the dead their nature too is not  universal as some cultures view them as  harmless or even good while others saw  them as malicious evil or dangerous  because of this it's hard to put a  definitive stamp on what they are and  what their purpose is in a lot of  western folklore they are said to be the  spirits of the dead who attempt to lure  people deeper into the marshes after  which they sink into the swamp and die  or become irreversibly lost never to be  seen again the lights are seen as  deceitful tricksters and those who come  across one should avoid giving into  temptation and attempt to follow it the  japanese oneibi and hitodama are the  closest thing to the will of the wisp  and even translated as such on some  occasions according to the folklore  onibi are spirits born from the corpses  of humans and animals they are also  described as being resentful and having  been transformed into fire a famous  encyclopedia compiled in 1712 describes  them as a blue light like a pine  torchlight and that humans who come too  close would have their spirits sucked  out of them similarly the hitodama are  said to be the spirits of the deceased  who take on the shape of a flame as with  the wisps they are deceitful and play  tricks on the living such as getting  travelers lost they commonly appear in  watery areas like wetlands but also  forests prairies and graveyards the  similarities between the ornibi hitodama  and the willow the wisp seems to suggest  that whatever people saw back in the day  they are describing the same type of  phenomena as for their explanation well  there have been many from glowing fungi  to fireflies glow worms and more the  lights observed inside marshes and  swamps have often been attributed to gas  rising up from the bogs mostly composed  of methane this gas is known to  sometimes spontaneously combust and  methane also just so happens to burn a  pale blue color in the case of the  graveyard lights the element phosphorus  which is abundant in human remains such  as teeth and bones is used as an  explanation it too can apparently ignite  during specific weather conditions  creating flames that linger for a while  funnily enough ever since modern science  has started finding rational  explanations for the phenomena sightings  of the will of the wisp have become  almost non-existent it's not exactly  clear why though some suggest that this  is because since the 1600s a lot of  marshland has disappeared due to human  intervention and graveyards that feature  open bone pits are no longer a common  practice either because of the dancing  or swaying motions of the lights when  observed from a distance people often  associated them with lanterns or torches  a flame moving around on its own as if  being carried around by an invisible  ghostly entity it is also from where the  most famous halloween decoration the  jack-o'-lantern got its inspiration for  these lights were seen all over the  world and documented in books used in  stories and fairy tales and of course  inevitably made their way into fiction  as well especially in fantasy and horror  one famous example are the dead marshes  featured in the lord of the rings an  ancient battlefield turned into a  haunted marshland where the corpses of  the dead are still submerged in its many  bogs and lakes similar to the stories of  the wisp the dead inside the marsh will  attempt to draw people in joining them  in death which is why gollum wisely says  lastly we have the japanese paper  lantern ghost though in this case it's  the lantern itself that has become a  sentient being rather than it being  carried by a ghostly figure or  representing its soul it's based on the  belief that inanimate objects can become  alive when they reach an old age and  although it does involve a lantern it's  likely not the inspiration for the  ghostly flames in the zelda series as  the idea doesn't apply to lanterns alone  though it could have inspired other  zelda enemies or themes which brings us  back to the games it's clear to me that  the pose their lanterns in the fiery  soul they leave behind are based on the  stories and legends of the will of the  wisp and similar myths the same goes for  a lot of the other ghostly phenomena  seen in the games whenever someone dies  or crosses over to the underworld their  soul can sometimes linger often taking  the form of a flame most commonly a pale  blue or greenish flame in this state  they cannot interact much with the world  of light a possible reason why the posts  carry their souls inside of a lantern is  to protect or guard it from their  enemies alternatively it could be a way  for them to manifest into a physical  body capable of interacting with the  world of the living by housing their  soul inside of a physical object they  gain a foothold in the physical plane a  great example of this aside from the  pose is the spirit of king rome boss  varamus hyrule he too is seen carrying a  lantern around whenever he takes on the  form of the old man but as soon as he  reveals his true identity the lantern  disappears and he takes on the form of  an apparition surrounded by flames as  such it's likely that his soul is stored  inside the lantern as a way to hide the  fact that he's a spirit as well as a way  to gain a physical presence ghosts and  spirits will likely always have their  place in the series whether it's an  apparition a shadow a spirit animal a  lingering flame or a vengeful monster it  all depends on what role they once  played and the emotional attachment they  have to the world they inhabit poles are  resentful filled with hatred and rage  and thus they turned into a monstrous  entity who seeks to do harm the flames  they carry are what binds them to the  world of the living their true essence  as soon as this essence is destroyed  they will either cease to exist in this  world or end up in a glass jar for sale  at your local pharmacy  and that concludes the video happy  halloween and to those celebrating this  year stay safe and have fun a big thanks  to conrad for joining me in this one you  can check out his halloween video by  clicking the end card or the link in the  description below as always many thanks  to my mods on discord and live streams  and to my generous patreons and channel  members you guys are and always will be  the best and that is all for now this is  dawn signing off and have a good one  [Music]  so  [Music]  you

